                            <comment id="16523602" author="jokser" created="Tue, 26 Jun 2018 11:41:23 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=pvinokurov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;pvinokurov&quot;&gt;pvinokurov&lt;/a&gt; I think that this fix is not completely correct because you&apos;re trying to fix the consequence that &apos;detectLostPartitions&apos; method is not idempotent.&lt;br/&gt;
I believe, that &apos;detectLostPartitions&apos; method should be reworked in a manner that partition is moved to LOST state only once (and the corresponding event is also fired once).&lt;br/&gt;
I also request to add a test to check when a cluster coordinator is failed during exchange with NODE_LEFT event and after that, no duplicate event is fired.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16524990" author="amashenkov" created="Wed, 27 Jun 2018 12:38:45 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=pvinokurov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;pvinokurov&quot;&gt;pvinokurov&lt;/a&gt;, please, fix code-styles, other looks good.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16525180" author="edshanggg" created="Wed, 27 Jun 2018 15:04:25 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=pvinokurov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;pvinokurov&quot;&gt;pvinokurov&lt;/a&gt;, What is about new test?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16525268" author="pvinokurov" created="Wed, 27 Jun 2018 16:38:13 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=EdShangGG&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;EdShangGG&quot;&gt;EdShangGG&lt;/a&gt; I modified test IgniteCachePartitionLossPolicySelfTest to check that the event is raised only once. Also I am working on test mentioned by Pavel Kovalenko.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16529453" author="pvinokurov" created="Mon, 2 Jul 2018 06:55:08 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=amashenkov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;amashenkov&quot;&gt;amashenkov&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=Jokser&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;jokser&quot;&gt;Jokser&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=EdShangGG&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;EdShangGG&quot;&gt;EdShangGG&lt;/a&gt; I have added a few tests including case of killing two nodes, killing a coordinator and cache with backup partitions. Please review&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16529498" author="edshanggg" created="Mon, 2 Jul 2018 07:56:21 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=pvinokurov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;pvinokurov&quot;&gt;pvinokurov&lt;/a&gt; Thank you!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I have several boring points. &lt;br/&gt;
Please, change the status the ticket to appropriate state.&lt;br/&gt;
Did you updated your TC Run All link? And where could we see your test in which TC configuration?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
